nio: mark the last steps of bsd_init on the panel

The photograph of run 594 shows bsd_init past the root mount,
past VFS_ROOT and devfs, and stopping after siginit.  siginit
itself is a short loop and cannot block; the boot is in one of
the calls that follow it, but those calls have no mark on the
panel.

Put direct-to-framebuffer checkpoints immediately after
siginit(), after bsd_utaskbootstrap(), and just before
load_init_program().  The next photograph will then say exactly
which of these steps the boot reaches and which one it does not
come back from.  No behaviour changes.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index 37b0174..97d3784 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -1239,9 +1239,11 @@ bsd_init(void)
 	/* Initialize signal state for process 0. */
 	bsd_init_kprintf("calling siginit\n");
 	siginit(kernproc);
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: CHK after siginit");
 
 	bsd_init_kprintf("calling bsd_utaskbootstrap\n");
 	bsd_utaskbootstrap();
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: CHK after utaskbootstrap");
 
 	pal_kernel_announce();
 
@@ -1321,6 +1323,7 @@ bsdinit_task(void)
 
 	bsd_init_kprintf("bsd_do_post - done");
 
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: CHK before load_init");
 	load_init_program(p);
 	lock_trace = 1;
 }
